<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gurbakhsh Singh (Kalsia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1760</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gurbakhsh Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> sardar of the Sandhu Jat clan from the village of Kalsia near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> and a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karorsinghia-misl">Karorsinghia</a> misl. Around 1760 he seized territory south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhachhrauli">Chhachhrauli</a>. His son Jodh Singh enlarged the holding, which became the princely state of Kalsia under British protection.</p></div>
